# Island: the input chain of input_chain.cir cut at the 5.3 V stage's output, which is a held node:
# everything behind it is one current source with the range that the part behind it takes over its
# own corners (input_chain.cir's `i(reg3v8.in)` plus the balancing divider: 94 uA..1.468 A). The
# parts behind are solved apart (a separate island) and the two ranges are joined here, so the
# combinations add up instead of multiplying: the price is that the load's current and the 5.3 V
# stage's output voltage are no longer tied to each other, which makes the answer wider.
# report: v(VIN5) i(f1) p(d2) i(reg5v3.in) p(reg5v3)
# today: the same as input_chain.cir
V  batt    VBATT GND 9..16
R  f1      VBATT FUSE_B 32m
D  d2      FUSE_B SAFE 0..0.8
R  r15     SAFE LOAD 50m+-1%
R  fb1     LOAD VIN5 0..70m
REG reg5v3 VIN5 V5 GND vout=5..5.5 eff=0.915..1 iq=20u vin_min=3
I  behind  V5 GND 93.8u..1.4679
